[1;33m[WARN][0m   Review: changes_requested (5 issue(s)) — The service-layer root-cause fix is correctly implemented — the live_preview config block (management_token, host, enable) is present in the Stack options object with CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN and CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST env vars destructured. This enables the Contentstack SDK to fetch draft/unpublished content when preview mode is active, partially satisfying AC #1 and #4. However, the implementation is incomplete for real-time preview: (1) No @contentstack/live-preview-utils dependency is installed, meaning no client-side WebSocket subscription to CMS entry-change events exists. (2) No reactive Provider component subscribes to onEntryChange, so useContent always returns static content — AC #2 (text changes appear without reload), AC #3 (link label/URL changes appear without reload), and AC #5 (consecutive edits appear in turn) are unmet. (3) No unit tests exist for the feature. (4) TypeScript strict violations (untyped any) are present in multiple locations. Verdict: changes_requested — the server-side fix is correct but the client-side reactivity mechanism and test coverage are required before merge.

